Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

(1) Start here: http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/  . Scroll down to the
section headed 'Fortify' and look at the three related functions for
converting spatial data frames or map files into a data frame object
that ggplot2 can handle. Also look at the help for geom_map().
(2) Look into the ggmap package by Dr. David Kahle, documented here:
journal.r-project.org/archive/2013-1/kahle-wickham.pdf <http://journal.r-project.org/archive/2013-1/kahle-wickham.pdf>
(3) Do a Google search on 'world map ggplot2'; there are more than a few hits.
(4) Do a search of the archives of this group; there are also more
than a few hits.

That should be enough to get you started on the way to graphing
map-related data in ggplot2.

Dennis

